 The pretrained PhIRE CNN and GAN provide fixed baselines. We use the released MR$\rightarrow$HR wind models of Stengel et al.~\cite{Stengel2020}, whose generator is a fully convolutional SRGAN-derived architecture with 16 residual blocks and skip connections; batch-normalization layers are omitted, and the wind network uses two input and output channels for the horizontal wind components. The CNN baseline is this generator after content-only pretraining with a pixelwise MSE loss; GAN training then continues from the pretrained generator with an additional discriminator and adversarial loss. We use the released checkpoints without retraining them. Every fine-tuned model starts from the pretrained CNN checkpoint and is fine-tuned for three epochs with Adam, learning rate $10^{-5}$, and batch size four, on the same 2688-field training set with the same normalization. All 16 configurations fine-tune the native PhIRE (TensorFlow) CNN generator itself; earlier experiments with separate PyTorch residual refiners were development studies and are excluded from this comparison. The \emph{reconstruction-only control} optimizes only the original vector reconstruction loss $L_{uv}$. The final topology-inspired objective and the 14 other loss configurations add auxiliary losses to $L_{uv}$ and are otherwise identical to the control. Differences between any configuration and the control therefore isolate the effect of its auxiliary losses from that of continued fine-tuning and additional data.
 
 \subsection{Reproducibility}
